  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39969176",
      "title": "JDBC Introduction",
      "lectureOrder": 121,
      "videoOrder": 120,
      "sourceHash": "9eadeb086ebb198774fe86cf9129dc0da7110c24140620ff8f5f981f649a633d",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.12,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "-: In this section we are going to talk about JDBC,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 8.13,
          "en": "which stands for Java Database Connectivity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.13,
          "end": 10.32,
          "en": "The thing is, if you think about software industry,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.32,
          "end": 11.76,
          "en": "it's all about data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.76,
          "end": 14.25,
          "en": "So whatever we do, we do it for data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.25,
          "end": 16.08,
          "en": "So even if you're building application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.08,
          "end": 18.96,
          "en": "you are building applications so that you can interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.96,
          "end": 22.59,
          "en": "with the data, storing data, fetching data, updating it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.59,
          "end": 23.76,
          "en": "and all kind of stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 26.22,
          "en": "Now till this point we have worked with data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.22,
          "end": 29.46,
          "en": "but all your data was getting stored in variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.46,
          "end": 32.76,
          "en": "Example, if you want to store a number, we were using int.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.76,
          "end": 36.09,
          "en": "If you want to store a point value, we were using double.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.09,
          "end": 39.15,
          "en": "The problem with that is what if you close your application?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.15,
          "end": 40.44,
          "en": "The moment you close the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.44,
          "end": 42.42,
          "en": "you will lose all your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 43.5,
          "en": "So what we want to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.5,
          "end": 46.44,
          "en": "is we want to store this data permanently somewhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.44,
          "end": 47.58,
          "en": "Of course there is one option,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 47.58,
          "end": 49.86,
          "en": "you can store your data in a normal file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 49.86,
          "end": 51.66,
          "en": "So maybe you can create a TXT file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 51.66,
          "end": 53.19,
          "en": "and store your data there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 53.19,
          "end": 55.29,
          "en": "But the problem is in TXT,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 55.29,
          "end": 57.69,
          "en": "it is very difficult to search certain things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 57.69,
          "end": 61.11,
          "en": "It's difficult to have relationship between two things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 61.11,
          "end": 63.93,
          "en": "Example, let's say if you are storing the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 63.93,
          "end": 65.04,
          "en": "and the age of a person,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 65.04,
          "end": 66.87,
          "en": "so let's say you have 10 person",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 66.87,
          "end": 70.35,
          "en": "and then each person will have their own name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 70.35,
          "end": 72.33,
          "en": "and their own age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 74.41499999999999,
          "en": "how will you search a particular age",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 74.41499999999999,
          "end": 75.6,
          "en": "for a particular person, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 75.6,
          "end": 77.31,
          "en": "It's very difficult in a text file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 77.31,
          "end": 78.81,
          "en": "So we have a way to solve this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 78.81,
          "end": 82.44,
          "en": "and that is your relational database management system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 82.44,
          "end": 86.46000000000001,
          "en": "So basically you can store your data in a Tableau format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 86.46000000000001,
          "end": 88.14,
          "en": "and that will be a permanent storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 88.14,
          "end": 91.41,
          "en": "Of course there are also some in-memory databases available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 91.41,
          "end": 92.82,
          "en": "but let's say by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 92.82,
          "end": 96.09,
          "en": "most of the DBMS are the permanent storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 96.09,
          "end": 98.13,
          "en": "So what you can do is you can store your data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 98.13,
          "end": 99.84,
          "en": "in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 99.84,
          "end": 103.11,
          "en": "The only problem is if you want to use this database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 103.11,
          "end": 105.15,
          "en": "you need to use SQL language,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 108.15,
          "en": "which is structured query language, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 108.15,
          "end": 111.75,
          "en": "So as a normal user, if I want to work with the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 111.75,
          "end": 114.09,
          "en": "I don't need to learn SQL, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 114.09,
          "end": 117.18,
          "en": "Of course you will not expect your client to learn SQL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 117.18,
          "end": 120.15,
          "en": "and that's why what you do is you have a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 120.15,
          "end": 122.52,
          "en": "but then between the user and a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 122.52,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "you'll be having an application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 127.02,
          "en": "Now this application can be built in any language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 127.02,
          "end": 128.73,
          "en": "Now since we're talking about Java,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 128.73,
          "end": 130.74,
          "en": "you can build this application between",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 130.74,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "with the help of Java language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 135.87,
          "en": "So a user can interact with the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 135.87,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "Now this is a console-based thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 140.1,
          "en": "so whatever we have done till now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 140.1,
          "end": 141.84,
          "en": "is all console-based, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 141.84,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "And the way a user can interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 146.1,
          "en": "with the console-based application is with the help of CMD.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 146.1,
          "end": 147.87,
          "en": "Maybe if you want to pass a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 147.87,
          "end": 149.52,
          "en": "maybe you want to get the value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 149.52,
          "end": 151.95,
          "en": "everything will be happening on that black screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 151.95,
          "end": 154.05,
          "en": "But what about the connection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 154.05,
          "end": 156.6,
          "en": "between the application and database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 156.6,
          "end": 159.51,
          "en": "and that's where we have to use some connectivity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 159.51,
          "end": 162.39,
          "en": "and that connectivity will be given by JDBC.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 162.39,
          "end": 164.97,
          "en": "Now JDBC is a API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 167.97,
          "en": "So it's a part of Java development kit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 167.97,
          "end": 171.27,
          "en": "So it gives you an API to connect with database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 171.27,
          "end": 173.22,
          "en": "But the problem is in this world,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 173.22,
          "end": 175.11,
          "en": "we don't have limited DBMS, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 176.91,
          "en": "We have lot of different databases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 176.91,
          "end": 181.86,
          "en": "Example, we have Oracle, PostgreSQL, MySQL, H2, DB2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 181.86,
          "end": 184.677,
          "en": "So we are going to use in this course Postgres.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 184.677,
          "end": 186.66,
          "en": "Now Postgres is very famous.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 186.66,
          "end": 188.85,
          "en": "Of course you can use any DBMS, which you like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 188.85,
          "end": 190.802,
          "en": "Personally, I prefer Postgres if given a choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 190.802,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "Otherwise, if a client says they already have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 196.56,
          "en": "some kind of DBMS installed, we will go for that one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 199.11,
          "en": "but we are going to use Postgres.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 199.11,
          "end": 201.42000000000002,
          "en": "Now the problem is as DBMS changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 201.42000000000002,
          "end": 203.82,
          "en": "don't you think this connectivity code will also change?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 203.82,
          "end": 205.47,
          "en": "Now we are saying that we have to connect Java",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 205.47,
          "end": 207.93,
          "en": "with the Postgres and it's working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 207.93,
          "end": 211.2,
          "en": "What if in future, you want to connect with MySQL?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 213.93,
          "en": "Now the problem is how many lines of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 213.93,
          "end": 215.37,
          "en": "you're going to change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 215.37,
          "end": 216.6,
          "en": "That's tricky, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 216.6,
          "end": 220.14,
          "en": "So what Java says is, okay, we have a JDBC API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 220.14,
          "end": 222.06,
          "en": "Now we will just give you interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 222.06,
          "end": 223.98,
          "en": "and few classes to work with,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 223.98,
          "end": 225.63,
          "en": "but the actual implementation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 225.63,
          "end": 228.57,
          "en": "will be given by the DBMS itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 228.57,
          "end": 231.78,
          "en": "So if Postgres says, okay, I have a DBMS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 231.78,
          "end": 234.18,
          "en": "and I'm allowing Java application to connect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 234.18,
          "end": 237.36,
          "en": "they have to provide the implementation for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 237.36,
          "end": 240.12,
          "en": "Same goes for MySQL, same goes for other companies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 240.12,
          "end": 241.56,
          "en": "So that means if you want to connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 241.56,
          "end": 243.15,
          "en": "your Java application with database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 243.15,
          "end": 245.16,
          "en": "of course you can use JDBC in Java,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 245.16,
          "end": 247.41,
          "en": "but you need actual implementation from DBMS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 247.41,
          "end": 249.84,
          "en": "So they will provide you some library to work with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 253.44,
          "en": "So in this particular series, we need to first make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 253.44,
          "end": 255.84,
          "en": "that you have your DBMS installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 255.84,
          "end": 257.37,
          "en": "We'll see that how would we do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 257.37,
          "end": 259.56,
          "en": "Next we also need a jar file the library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 259.56,
          "end": 262.32,
          "en": "to connect this two and how to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 262.32,
          "end": 264.273,
          "en": "we'll see in the upcoming videos.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
